# Line endings.
#
# The repository is uniformly LF and Prettier pins `endOfLine: "lf"`. Windows
# checkouts would otherwise convert on checkout and convert back on commit,
# which mostly works until it doesn't — a stray CRLF turns a one-line change
# into a whole-file diff and buries the actual edit.
#
# Normalising here means the rule travels with the repository instead of
# depending on every developer's local git configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be touched.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary

# The frozen legacy product. Kept byte-for-byte as the reference it is, and
# excluded from diffs so it never drowns a review — it is one 400KB line.
_reference/** -diff linguist-vendored

# Generated, and noise in review.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
